From bd97b82c28eadb83fb80b0004836c1f26d633e92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TorrServerManager <noreply@torrservermanager.local>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 23:11:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] gstreamer: make the task lock context-aware and add
 LeaseSegment

Task.mu was a plain sync.Mutex, so a cancelled request would still wait its
turn and then run a full seek nobody needed. Replace it with a buffered
channel gate whose lock(ctx) gives up as soon as ctx is done, and check ctx
before seeking in seekToSegmentLocked instead of only after the work is done.

LeaseSegment takes the segment lease under the gate and returns it after the
gate is released, so the caller can write the response without holding the
task lock for the duration of the network write.
